From d5840e0e95eebfd9eb067c3e92a2f5461f0217bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabio <fabio@git.it>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:39:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] serve s3: use less memory and CPU with big objects on small
 hosts (backport)

Patch of the fork proposed to upstream, carried as
webui/backports/07-serve-s3-small-hosts.patch: it is the squash of the
serve s3 commits of the fork, documented in fork-doc/serve-s3.md.

- don't read the whole object to hash it on HEAD and GET when its ETag
  is kept, nor every few minutes once the VFS directory cache expires
- fix multipart uploads failing with InvalidPart when a part request
  timed out while the buffered parts after it were being written
- write buffered parts in the background, so a part request no longer
  waits for the parts after it
- use less memory to remember the parts of big multipart objects
- add --temp-object-expiry to remove on startup the temporary objects
  left by a crash
- document the memory and disk space needed with big objects

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
